The LIGO Scientific Collaboration's Gravitational Wave Open Data project offers publicly accessible data from LIGO and Virgo detectors, as well as coalescing compact binaries, for use in the community. To facilitate analysis of these data sets, we have developed a collection of 23 Octave functions, known as OctApps, which provide tools for examining ongoing gravitational wave data. These functions, including visualization and analysis tools, are designed to be user-friendly and can be executed directly within the browser via the Gravitational Wave Open Data platform, eliminating the need for local software installation. Additionally, we provide a comprehensive user guide for Octave, enabling users to leverage these tools in data exploration. OctApps are freely available online. 

